<title>ETHIOPIA: Addis Ababa shop owners protest against rents.</title>
<headline>Addis Ababa shop owners protest against rents.</headline>
<dateline>ADDIS ABABA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Up to 70,000 shop owners staged a rally in the Ethiopian capital on Thursday to protest against rent hikes by Prime Minister Meles Zenawi on state-owned property.</p>
<p>Demonstrators waved placards and banners and were expected to hand in a petition at Zenawi's office.</p>
<p>Zenawi described as &quot;just and fair&quot; last week the recent price adjustments by Addis Ababa City Council, which provide new agreements for 21,000 traders.</p>
<p>Addis Ababa was virtually paralysed during the first demonstration against the rent hikes on September 3, but residents said some shops remained open on Thursday.</p>
</text>
